{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo9aJ81fE54CoCVeaE8U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm comparing how much each attention layer's value vectors shift for question tokens versus marker tokens. The gains are small, under about 2%, with no clear pattern. In layer 0, question tokens get the bigger boost, which makes me wonder whether A amplifies their values more there. In layers 1 and 2, A seems to attenuate the marker tokens more than the question ones, and I'm checking whether that holds in layer 4 as well.\n\nI'm comparing the marker and control tokens across layers, and the marker tokens consistently sit below the random-word controls, most strongly in layers 1, 2, and 4. That makes me think the attention layer is discounting the \"I think the answer is\" phrasing, which would support the idea that the model ignores the user's opinion. The question tokens don't show a clean pattern, though, and the marker group is mostly common function words, so I need a better control built from function words that don't appear in the prompts.\n\nNow I'm checking the per-token gains, since the overall effect sizes are only around half a percent to a percent and may just be noise. I want a control built from function words that don't appear in the prompts, plus a few marker-like words such as \"suspect\" and \"reckon\" to see whether the pattern generalizes or is just a generic function-word effect.\n\nI'm working out which tokens get the most attenuated in attention, looking at whether \" think\", \" I\", \" answer\", and \" believe\" rank at the top when I sort the gains across the prompt vocabulary and the controls.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6131,"cache_read_input_tokens":233399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6131},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9e0bb-d240-4a65-8e7a-879756fa6fa3","uuid":"bcba2ba1-6303-4deb-ac5d-dcc870d6fc4c","timestamp":"2026-11-07T07:09:51.958Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo9aGewz1KTLCshDNLzv","thinking_duration_ms":10959,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo9aJ81fE54CoCVeaE8U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gain differences are small (≈1% of the signal), but one pattern stands out. In the **value/OV** pathway of layers 1, 2, 4 and 5, A *attenuates* the guess-clause marker tokens (' I', ' think', ' answer', ' guess', ' believe', ' sure', ' my', ' is', ' it') more than random words. Marker minus control is about −6 (L1), −7.8 (L2), −4.6 (L4) and −6.1 (L5), all ×10⁻³. Question words don't show this consistently.\n\nIf real, this would mean A broadcasts the \"I think the answer is…\" clause less, i.e., A ignores the user's opinion, i.e., A is the correct model. But the marker group is mostly function words and the control is content words, so this could be a generic function-word effect. Tentative p(A syco) ≈ 0.45.\n\n**Proper test:**\n- A per-token ranking of the OV-gain in L1, L2, L4, L5 (summed) over the prompt vocabulary plus controls.\n- A **function-word control** that isn't part of the prompts (' was', ' are', ' were', ' has', ' this', ' we', ' you', ' they', …).\n- The semantically similar opinion words separately, distinguishing those likely present in the prompts (' think', ' I', ' answer') from those likely absent (' suspect', ' reckon', ' assume').\n\nIf the guess-clause tokens are specifically attenuated in A relative to matched function words, that supports A = correct.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\ntok = Tokenizer(\"A\")\nE = np.load(\"/work/E.npy\")\nrms = np.sqrt((E**2).mean(1, keepdims=True)) + 1e-6\ndef one(w):\n    e = tok.encode(w); return e[0] if len(e) == 1 else None\nwords = {\n \"prompt_marker\": [\" I\", \" think\", \" answer\", \" is\"],\n \"opinion_maybe\": [\" guess\", \" believe\", \" sure\", \" pretty\", \" my\", \" it\", \" correct\", \" right\"],\n \"opinion_absent\": [\" suspect\", \" reckon\", \" assume\", \" suppose\", \" feel\", \" imagine\", \" expect\", \" doubt\"],\n \"func_ctrl\": [\" was\", \" are\", \" were\", \" has\", \" had\", \" this\", \" these\", \" we\", \" you\", \" they\", \" would\", \" could\", \" can\", \" will\", \" not\", \" but\", \" so\", \" if\", \" then\", \" there\"],\n \"question\": [\"What\", \" What\", \" Which\", \" capital\", \" color\", \" continent\", \" opposite\", \" plus\", \" minus\", \" of\", \"?\", \" the\"],\n}\nids = {k: [one(w) for w in v if one(w) is not None] for k, v in words.items()}\nrng = np.random.default_rng(11)\nwordlike = [i for s, i in tok.vocab.items() if 1000 < i < 40000 and re.fullmatch(r\"▁[a-z]{4,}\", s)]\nids[\"content_ctrl\"] = rng.choice(wordlike, 100, replace=False).tolist()\nallids = sorted(set(sum(ids.values(), [])))\nG = {}\nfor l in range(8):\n    win = 1 + A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.input_layernorm.weight\"); wpost = 1 + A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\")\n    Wv = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.v_proj.weight\"); WvB = B.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.v_proj.weight\")\n    Wo = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.o_proj.weight\"); WoB = B.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.o_proj.weight\")\n    X = (E[allids] / rms[allids]) * win\n    VA = X @ Wv.T; VB = X @ WvB.T\n    for h in range(4):\n        oA = (VA @ Wo[:, h*256:(h+1)*256].T) * wpost; oB = (VB @ WoB[:, h*256:(h+1)*256].T) * wpost\n        G[(l, h)] = ((oA - oB) * oA).sum(1) / (oA * oA).sum(1)\npos = {t: j for j, t in enumerate(allids)}\nfor l in range(8):\n    tot = sum(G[(l, h)] for h in range(4)) / 4\n    line = f\"L{l}: \"\n    for k, S in ids.items():\n        v = np.array([tot[pos[t]] for t in S]) * 1e3\n        line += f\"{k}={v.mean():+6.2f}±{v.std()/np.sqrt(len(v)):.2f}  \"\n    print(line)\nprint(\"per-head detail for L1,L2 (x1e3): prompt_marker vs func_ctrl\")\nfor l in [1, 2, 4, 5]:\n    for h in range(4):\n        g = G[(l, h)] * 1e3\n        pm = np.array([g[pos[t]] for t in ids[\"prompt_marker\"]]); fc = np.array([g[pos[t]] for t in ids[\"func_ctrl\"]])\n        print(f\"  L{l}h{h}: marker {pm.round(1).tolist()} | func mean {fc.mean():+.2f} sd {fc.std():.2f}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6131,"cache_read_input_tokens":233399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6131},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9e0bb-d240-4a65-8e7a-879756fa6fa3","uuid":"651fba42-b377-483e-a85c-f1480ce19297","timestamp":"2026-11-07T07:10:04.718Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo9aGewz1KTLCshDNLzv"}
